  "body": "**Stacked on #973** (branch `issue/938-tilt-tolerance` @ 9b01def4, which already carries current `main`). This PR's own change is the single commit de1d8641; until #973 merges the diff against `main` also shows #973's commits. Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nSince #938 a pose within 1e-9 rad is judged upright. Just above it the reach laws took the tilted column, which stood each band's bottom one **whole radius** under its foot. An r 12 holder 5 mm clear of a part was clean at 1e-9 rad and `ShankHit { part: true }` at 2e-9 rad or 0.01 degrees.\n\nThe tilted column now dips by the rim's exact `R·sin θ`. One helper, `verify::tilt_band::lean` (new module `crates/sim/src/verify/tilt_band.rs`), builds the column; the four copies of the formula are gone. Consumers:\n\n| Law | File | Was | Now |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| (c) reach vs rest material | `reach.rs` | bottom `- R` | bottom `- R·sin θ` |\n| (c3) mid-turn sweep | `sweep.rs` | bottom `- R` | bottom `- R·sin θ` |\n| (c2) fixture band column | `stack_span.rs` | z planes `-/+ R` | `-/+ R·sin θ` |\n| (d2) tilted rapid, flute column | `laws.rs` | z planes `-/+ R` | `-/+ R·sin θ` |\n\nThe column's centre and radius are the sums they were. Every upright branch is untouched. The posed capsule sweep, the mesh-steel law, the solid law and the contact law place the real pose and do not share this column; they are not changed.\n\n## Derivation (full text in `docs/decisions/1303-tilt-band-dip.md`)\n\nA band is the cylinder of radius R about the unit axis `a` (tilted θ off +Z) between axial stations `above` and `above + len`: points `tip + s·a + ρ·w`, `0 <= ρ <= R`, `w` a unit vector square to `a`.\n\n- **z.** Write +Z as `cos θ·a + sin θ·h` with `h` unit and square to `a`. Then `w·Z = sin θ·(w·h)`, at most `sin θ`, reached at the rim point `w = ±h`. The axial part `s·az` is linear, so its extremes are the two ends. Lowest point: `tip.z + min(above·az, (above+len)·az) - R·sin θ`; highest: `max(..) + R·sin θ`. Both ends are in the `min`/`max`, so the band's own height is included.\n- **Sideways** (unchanged): `s·a` stays within `len/2·sin θ` of the mid-station's foot and the disc adds R or less, so radius `R + len/2·sin θ` about `mid·(ax, ay)` holds it.\n\n**Never under.** `rim_sine` = `min(1, max(h, h/|a|))`, `h = hypot(ax, ay)`: the sine itself for a unit axis, the larger reading for an axis off unit length, and 1 (the old whole radius) for a zero or non-finite axis. Never more than the old reading, never less than the true dip.\n\n## Verdicts and goldens that moved\n\n- Tilted moves only, toward clean only, and only where the old extra depth (between `R·sin θ` and `R`) was what met the material.\n- `crates/sim/tests/tilt_tolerance.rs` (#938's pins): `a_tilt_just_above_the_tolerance_is_still_judged_tilted` expected the r 15 holder 5 mm over the stock to convict at 1.01e-9 rad and 0.001 degrees. That was the cliff. It is now `a_tilt_just_above_the_tolerance_reads_like_upright_and_a_real_dip_convicts` (clean at both, convicted at 20 degrees where the rim is 1.9 mm into the stock). `a_leaning_shank_and_holder_report_one_shank_hit_per_move` moved its tilt to 20 degrees so the holder group still convicts beside the shank group.\n- No golden, no posted output, no other existing test changed.\n\n## How tested\n\nPins (new):\n- `crates/app/tests/tilt_band_dip.rs`, on the `beside_wall` plate:\n  - `a_small_tilt_of_a_holder_standing_clear_over_the_part_no_longer_convicts` - 1e-9, 2e-9 rad, 0.01 and 1 degree clean;\n  - `a_tilt_that_brings_the_rim_into_the_part_still_convicts` - 0.4 degrees clean (rim 0.016 mm clear), 0.6, 1, 2, 5, 10, 30, 60 degrees `ShankHit { part: true }`;\n  - `the_verdict_is_monotone_in_the_tilt_across_the_upright_tolerance` - 20 tilts from 0 to 60 degrees, clean then convicted, never back, turning between 0.4 and 0.6 degrees;\n  - `the_mid_turn_sweep_dips_by_the_rim_too` - law (c3).\n- `verify::tilt_band` unit tests: a 4000-case property (random tilt 0..180 degrees, azimuth, R, foot, length; every sampled band point inside the column, and the column's planes reached by the samples), the limits, the unreadable-axis fallback, and the (c2) column read directly.\n\nMutation check, by hand: the whole radius (old reading) fails all four app pins; half the dip (an under-read) fails the conviction pins and the property test.\n\nGate on de1d8641, local:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: sim suites ok, motion suites ok, app suites ok (190 s), 0 failed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-sim`: 59 binaries ok, 486 passed, 0 failed.\n- app `tilt_band_dip`, `tool_body_bands`, `tool_body_judged`, `sim_tool_body`, `verify`, `posed_contact`, `rotary_verify`, `solid_law`, `solid_law_goldens`: 76 passed, 0 failed.\n- motion `multiaxis`, `multiaxis_avoid`, `multiaxis_rough`, `swarf_pose_continuity`, `swarf_reentry`, `pivot5d`: 33 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised / known\n\n- Batch and release tiers and the `--ignored` heavy lanes were not run.\n- The fixture verdict on a posed move is still the OR of the column and the posed capsule sweep, whose capsules reach a whole radius past each band end. A clamp just under a holder is still convicted on any tilt above the tolerance (`the_fixture_band_law_reads_noise_as_upright_and_a_real_tilt_as_tilted` is unchanged). Filed as #1305.\n- Law (c3) still samples the turn (4 stations x 5 pose fractions). The decision file argues the sampled bottoms bound the in-between ones in z; that argument is not pinned by a test.\n- No hands-on check in the GUI or on a machine.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nChangelog: A tilted tool's holder and shank bands are enclosed by the rim's exact dip (R·sin θ) instead of the whole radius, so a small commanded tilt no longer reports a false shank or fixture-column collision (#1303)\n\nFixes #1303\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
